  "worked_solution": "We solve the inequality just like we would solve an equation.\n\nFirst, we apply the addition principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4u-11 & \\ge 9u+4 \\\\ 4u-11-9u & \\ge 9u+4-9u \\\\ -11-5u & \\ge 4 \\\\ -11-5u+11 & \\ge 4+11 \\\\ -5u & \\ge 15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the multiplication principle.\n\nRemember, when we divide an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5u & \\ge 15 \\\\ \\frac{-5u}{-5} & \\,\\,\\le \\,\\,\\frac{15}{-5} \\\\ u & \\le -3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
